# Generated / large
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
out/
*.egg-info/

# Synthetic datasets: the .gwy pairs are large (~1 MB per sample) and fully
# reproducible from tools/make_dataset.py given the seed recorded in
# summary.json. Track the labels and the summary, not the pixels.
data/**/clean/
data/**/degraded/
data/smoketest/

# Keep the API inventory and the data survey - they are deliverables,
# not build artifacts.

# The map from scan-0NN back to the original filenames. Those names carry
# collaborators' names and unpublished samples, and this repository is public.
# It stays on the machine that made the corpus; export/scans/ itself is
# committed, and nothing in it can be traced back without this file.
export/original-names.json

# And the list of which originals matter and why. Each entry pairs a real
# filename with a reason that also appears in baseline.json beside a scan id --
# publish both halves and the mapping reassembles itself.
export/argued-about.json

# The owner's own labels for 31 scans, keyed by the original filenames and
# describing what each sample is. Nothing in the code reads it; it is reference
# for whoever is working, and it belongs on the machine, not on a public repo.
# data/reference_samples.json stays tracked -- that one is the owner's own
# catalog with no third party in it, and it is the acceptance test.
data/real_labels.json

# External raw-data audits are private; never commit outputs or raw inputs.
AFM_Copilot_Private_Audits/
PRIVATE_manifest.csv
PRIVATE_probe_job.json
CHATGPT_REVIEW.zip
